type: software
title: "Ramanujan's 1/π Series and Harmonic Numbers: Proof and Verification"
authors:
  - name: "Open"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A proof, with computer verification, of Conjecture 1 from MathOverflow
  question 507693: for the rational hypergeometric Ramanujan 1/π series,
  sum f'(n) = 2πi τ~ sum f(n), so Re sum f'(n) = -2π Im(τ) sum f(n).
  The identity holds on the imaginary axis above i/√N and on the line
  Re τ = 1/2, without complex multiplication; the 36 convergent series of
  the Cohen–Guillera table are a corollary. The proof relies on cited
  published results and is not peer reviewed.
